{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgBzoDVsjE1xSwdzaYDiy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Short answer:** A component calls `useSession()` from `@openmrs/esm-react-utils`. The hook never returns `null`. It either returns a `Session` or suspends while the session loads. When nobody is logged in, the session is `{ authenticated: false, sessionId: '' }`, so components check `session.authenticated` rather than testing for null.\n\n**How the read works**\n\n- The hook suspends (throws a promise) until the global session store has loaded, then returns the session and subscribes to later changes. `openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-react-utils/src/useSession.ts:17-116`\n- The store itself is a global store named `session`, starting as `{ loaded: false, session: null }`. `openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-api/src/current-user.ts:29-32`\n- `getSessionStore()` kicks off a refresh if the session is missing or older than 60 seconds, then returns the store. `openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-api/src/current-user.ts:64-74` and `:164-167`\n- The session comes from `refetchCurrentUser()`, which calls the session endpoint. `openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-api/src/current-user.ts:251-277`\n\n**What happens when nobody is authenticated**\n\n- A 401 or 403 from the session endpoint is treated as \"not logged in\", not as a failed lookup. The store records `{ loaded: true, session: { authenticated: false, ... } }`, or clears to that state if the body isn't a session. `openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-api/src/current-user.ts:567-602` and `:604-606`, `:634-636`\n- `clearCurrentUser()` sets the unauthenticated session explicitly, for example on logout. `openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-api/src/current-user.ts:291-299`\n- Other failures are recorded as errors. If a session had already loaded, the last good one is kept. `openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-api/src/current-user.ts:567-602`\n- A 403 from the session endpoint triggers the configured auth-failure redirect (to login) unless the caller passes `rejectAuthFailure`. `openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-api/src/openmrs-fetch.ts:225-243`\n- The app shell only starts optional dependencies once `session.authenticated` is true. `openmrs-esm-core/packages/shell/esm-app-shell/src/events.ts:9-20`\n- The login app's `RedirectLogout` component checks `session.authenticated` and navigates to the login route when it is false. `openmrs-esm-core/packages/apps/esm-login-app/src/redirect-logout/redirect-logout.component.tsx:8-52`\n\n**Documentation**\n\n- `useSession` API reference: `openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-framework/docs/functions/useSession.md:3-13`. It says the hook returns `authenticated == false` when not logged in, uses Suspense, and never returns `null`.\n- Session fields available to extension expressions (`authenticated`, `user`, `sessionLocation`, and so on): `openmrs-contrib-o3-docs/content/en-US/docs/extension-system.mdx:154-159`\n- Session helpers listed among core concepts: `openmrs-contrib-o3-docs/content/en-US/docs/core-concepts.mdx:189`\n\n**Example component in the chart**\n\n`openmrs-esm-patient-chart/packages/esm-patient-orders-app/src/print/print.component.tsx:17-21` calls `useSession()` inside a function component. Other chart components do the same, for example `packages/esm-patient-notes-app/src/notes/visit-notes-form.component.tsx:160`.\n\n**Caveats**\n\n- Falkon has no repository named \"O3 frontend\". I took the frontend to mean the O3 framework in `openmrs-esm-core` plus the patient-chart apps that consume it.\n- I did not read the `Session` type definition, the `redirectAuthFailure` default configuration, or the shell code that triggers the initial session load. The search budget ran out before I could check them.\n\n```json\n[\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-react-utils/src/useSession.ts\", \"startLine\": 17, \"endLine\"