app/src/redirect-logout/redirect-logout.component.tsx:8-52`\n\n**Documentation**\n\n- `useSession` API reference: `openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-framework/docs/functions/useSession.md:3-13`. It says the hook returns `authenticated == false` when not logged in, uses Suspense, and never returns `null`.\n- Session fields available to extension expressions (`authenticated`, `user`, `sessionLocation`, and so on): `openmrs-contrib-o3-docs/content/en-US/docs/extension-system.mdx:154-159`\n- Session helpers listed among core concepts: `openmrs-contrib-o3-docs/content/en-US/docs/core-concepts.mdx:189`\n\n**Example component in the chart**\n\n`openmrs-esm-patient-chart/packages/esm-patient-orders-app/src/print/print.component.tsx:17-21` calls `useSession()` inside a function component. Other chart components do the same, for example `packages/esm-patient-notes-app/src/notes/visit-notes-form.component.tsx:160`.\n\n**Caveats**\n\n- Falkon has no repository named \"O3 frontend\". I took the frontend to mean the O3 framework in `openmrs-esm-core` plus the patient-chart apps that consume it.\n- I did not read the `Session` type definition, the `redirectAuthFailure` default configuration, or the shell code that triggers the initial session load. The search budget ran out before I could check them.\n\n```json\n[\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-react-utils/src/useSession.ts\", \"startLine\": 17, \"endLine\": 116},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-api/src/current-user.ts\", \"startLine\": 567, \"endLine\": 602},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-api/src/current-user.ts\", \"startLine\": 164, \"endLine\": 167},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-api/src/current-user.ts\", \"startLine\": 251, \"endLine\": 277},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-api/src/current-user.ts\", \"startLine\": 291, \"endLine\": 299},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-ap